      "message": "I updated both files:\n\n- **`src/format.js`**: Added an exported `round2(n)` helper, which rounds to 2 decimals using `Number.EPSILON` so values like `1.005` round to `1.01`. `money()` now calls it before formatting. Previously it used `toFixed(2)` directly, which can round `1.005` down to `$1.00`.\n- **`src/cart.js`**: Imports `round2` from `./format.js`. `total()` and `applyDiscount()` now return rounded values. Before, they returned raw floating-point results.\n\nA quick smoke test gave `money(1.005)` → `$1.01`, `total([0.1, 0.2])` → `0.3`, and `applyDiscount(19.99, 15)` → `16.99`. I didn't run the project's test suite, since I didn't find one in this check.\n\nOne thing I noticed but left alone: `total([])` returns `NaN`, because `sum` starts as `undefined` and the `+ 0` at the end doesn't fix it. That was already true before my change, and it's outside the rounding task. Say if you want it fixed to return `0`.",
